  "content": "Cancer Free Since 2019Radical Remission ProjectMay 29, 20241 min readRomy was diagnosed with Stage IV colon cancer in October 2014. In the first 4 years, she had 8 surgeries, 7 recurrences, chemo, and radiation. In her gut, she never actually thought this was going to take her out, but since everyone was telling her it would, she forged ahead. Around the 3-year mark she added in several other modalities to improve her outcome. She really feels that releasing suppressed emotions and having a strong will to live changed her outcome dramatically. January of 2024 marks 5 years of No Evidence of Disease.To learn more from Romy...Instagram - @tobecontinued.podcast or @wighthorseFacebook - wighthorsecharityWebsite - www.wighthorse.comListen to Romy's story and others like it here.818818 views00 commentsPost not marked as liked",
